Subject to the conditions below, the Project grants You a worldwide,
royalty-free, non-exclusive license to:

  (a) use and run the Covered Work;
  (b) study the Covered Work and how it works;
  (c) modify the Covered Work and create improvements and derivatives;
  (d) redistribute the Covered Work and your modifications, in source form,
      to the community.

This is a license to build with, learn from, and improve the Covered Work
together. You are encouraged to contribute your improvements back to the
Project (see Section 7).

================================================================================
4. CONDITIONS
================================================================================

Every exercise of the rights in Section 3 is subject to all of the following:

  4.1  NON-COMMERCIAL. You may not sell, charge for, or otherwise commercially
       exploit the Covered Work, access to it, or anything made accessible
       through it. You may not use the Covered Work in a commercial setting
       (including arcades, kiosks, or paid entertainment venues) without
       explicit written permission from the Project.

  4.2  SHARE ALIKE. If You distribute the Covered Work or any modification of
       it, You must do so in source form and under this same license. Keep it
       open; do not relicense it or close it off.

  4.3  ATTRIBUTION. You must retain all copyright notices, attributions, and
       Project branding in the Covered Work. You may add your own attribution
       for your contributions; you may not remove or misrepresent the
       Project's.

  4.4  NO GATEKEEPING. You may not place the Covered Work, or any derivative,
       behind a paywall, a required donation, a subscription, or any other
       barrier to access.

  4.5  STATE CHANGES. If You modify a file, say so plainly in the file or in an
       accompanying note, so others can tell your work from the original.

================================================================================
5. CLEAN-ROOM / NO GAME CONTENT
================================================================================

The Covered Work is original, clean-room development. It contains no
copyrighted game code, no extracted game assets, and no proprietary firmware
from any third party. It speaks to arcade hardware protocols and operating
system interfaces; it does not include, embed, or distribute any game files.

You must keep it that way. Do not contribute, add, or distribute copyrighted
game code, extracted assets, or third-party proprietary firmware as part of the
Covered Work. Any contribution containing such material will be rejected and
removed. The sourcing and legality of game files is solely the responsibility
of the end user, as described in the EULA.

================================================================================
6. THE PROJECT'S COMMITMENT
================================================================================

These are promises to the community. They are not a disclaimer of your rights;
they are a statement of intent that the Project asks every contributor to
honor:

  - Ultra Loader will always be free to download and use. No subscription, no
    paywall, no tier system, ever.
  - No game access will ever be paywalled. Every user gets the same software
    with the same capabilities.
  - No donations are required or solicited as a condition of use.
  - All research and development is returned to the community at no cost.

